WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.060
- This is not chai.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.526
This is a chai tea latte.

00:00:02.526 --> 00:00:04.489
And look at how they spelled my name.

00:00:04.489 --> 00:00:05.365
Emme?

00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:07.744
(laughs) We're not gonna go get this.

00:00:07.744 --> 00:00:11.595
♫ If you see something

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:12.539
♫ You better

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:13.432
- Hey, guys!

00:00:13.432 --> 00:00:14.539
I'm Ahmed Ali Akbar.

00:00:14.539 --> 00:00:16.650
I'm the host of See
Something Say Something,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.009
Buzzfeed's show where we tell life stories

00:00:19.009 --> 00:00:20.945
and talk about being Muslim in America.

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:22.650
It's very cold out here in New York,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.225
and we are gonna go find
a good hot cup of chai.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.584
We're gonna be joined
by our cab driver Jamil.

00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:30.222
I'm gonna go to Brooklyn,
pick up my sister,

00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:32.405
then we're gonna go to three chai places

00:00:32.405 --> 00:00:34.480
and sample the stuff they have there.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.098
To you, what is chai?

00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:37.325
- It's a part of life, you know?

00:00:37.325 --> 00:00:38.637
It's hard to quit that, you know?

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.514
- Yes.

00:00:39.514 --> 00:00:40.578
Definitely addicting.

00:00:40.578 --> 00:00:41.649
Do you like cardamom in your tea?

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:42.730
- No.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:43.563
- Wow.

00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:45.275
So you're very milk, sugar.
- Just milk, sugar,

00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:46.108
and that's it.

00:00:46.108 --> 00:00:47.537
- Zainab, how obsessed with chai are you?

00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:49.063
We are not about chai tea lattes.

00:00:49.063 --> 00:00:50.368
- No!

00:00:50.368 --> 00:00:51.748
Chai means tea,

00:00:51.748 --> 00:00:55.735
so a chai tea latte is a tea tea milk.

00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:57.747
- That's what I told you.
- Chai is tea with milk.

00:00:57.747 --> 00:00:59.873
- So, we're gonna go to three places.

00:00:59.873 --> 00:01:02.000
My favorite place is Chandni.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.179
Zainab, your favorite place is?

00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:04.634
- [Zainab] Punjabi Deli, whoop whoop!

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.066
- [Ahmed] And Jamil?
- [Jamil] I go to Haandi.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.396
- You go to Haandi.

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:08.425
We're gonna compare all three,

00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:10.343
decide which one is the best cheap,

00:01:10.343 --> 00:01:12.687
delicious, tasty chai.

00:01:12.687 --> 00:01:13.520
- Let's do it.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.356
(energetic music)

00:01:15.356 --> 00:01:16.556
- Ever since I started
working at Buzzfeed,

00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:20.444
I will go to Chandni and
grab two cups of chai,

00:01:20.444 --> 00:01:22.358
and I would give it to my coworkers.

00:01:22.358 --> 00:01:24.339
I had somebody describe to me,

00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:26.697
which, not inaccurately, but
I wouldn't have thought of it,

00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:27.907
as brothy.

00:01:27.907 --> 00:01:28.740
- Huh.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.804
(energetic music)

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:34.119
- So, we're here at Chandni in Manhattan.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:36.828
We're here with the chef
of Chandni, Muhammad.

00:01:36.828 --> 00:01:37.992
How do you make your chai?

00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:40.210
- Water, milk, spices,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.997
pour tea inside, and that's it.

00:01:41.997 --> 00:01:42.920
Tea is ready.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.420
(funky music)

00:01:47.918 --> 00:01:50.425
- [Ahmed] (chuckling) That is gorgeous.

00:01:50.425 --> 00:01:51.940
- This is international recipe.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.255
I learned from my mother.

00:01:53.255 --> 00:01:54.949
- As all good recipes come.

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:56.024
I just learned so much.

00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:57.933
I mean, I've seen it, but not like that.

00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:00.642
That was on next level stuff.

00:02:00.642 --> 00:02:01.849
Oh my God.

00:02:01.849 --> 00:02:02.682
- It's magical.

00:02:02.682 --> 00:02:03.730
- It hits you so right away.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.563
- It's perfect.

00:02:04.563 --> 00:02:05.632
- Every sip is just like,

00:02:05.632 --> 00:02:07.237
it's got spice, it's got cream.

00:02:07.237 --> 00:02:08.432
- Oh, it's like, silky.

00:02:08.432 --> 00:02:09.824
- And a lot of sugar.

00:02:09.824 --> 00:02:11.036
I know you don't drink sugar.

00:02:11.036 --> 00:02:14.081
- Regularly, I don't actually,
you know, as a routine.

00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:15.491
If it comes, that's okay, doesn't matter.

00:02:15.491 --> 00:02:16.752
- What would you rate it out of five?

00:02:16.752 --> 00:02:19.289
- Definitely, I'm gonna go four for that,

00:02:19.289 --> 00:02:21.042
because I don't drink with...

00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:23.666
I mean, cinnamon and the laung,
that other thing, you know?

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:25.128
It's not my taste, actually, for that.

00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:26.959
But no doubt, it's a very good tea.

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:29.710
- I would give it a five out of five.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.186
- I would give it a four
because it's too sweet for me.

00:02:32.186 --> 00:02:33.019
- That's good by me.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.473
I'm happy with that.

00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:36.303
All right, let's go to Punjabi Deli.

00:02:36.303 --> 00:02:37.555
- Let's do it!
- That's our next stop.

00:02:37.555 --> 00:02:40.805
(Middle Eastern music)

00:02:49.325 --> 00:02:52.170
(inhales and sighs)
Yes, it smells so good.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.368
- Smells like home!
- It's very comforting.

00:02:54.368 --> 00:02:55.201
I'm Ahmed.

00:02:55.201 --> 00:02:56.110
- Okay.
- Nice to meet you.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:56.943
Your name is?

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.289
- My name is Kulwinder Singh.
- Kulwinder Singh.

00:02:59.289 --> 00:03:00.539
What do you put in your chai?

00:03:00.539 --> 00:03:04.335
- In our tea, we put half
water, half of the milk,

00:03:04.335 --> 00:03:07.981
and then we add in
cardamom, ginger, cinnamon.

00:03:07.981 --> 00:03:09.465
We have also the cloves.

00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:11.142
You will really enjoy this tea.

00:03:11.142 --> 00:03:12.453
- [Ahmed] So, did you always make it

00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:14.129
with the espresso machine?

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:14.962
- Yeah.

00:03:14.962 --> 00:03:16.573
It's always working 24 hours.

00:03:16.573 --> 00:03:17.802
As a taxi.

00:03:17.802 --> 00:03:18.937
- [Ahmed] Like a taxi.

00:03:18.937 --> 00:03:21.221
Are most of your customers taxi drivers?

00:03:21.221 --> 00:03:22.054
- Yeah.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.059
- Oh, it tastes so good.

00:03:26.059 --> 00:03:29.526
- I feel like the difference
between this and Chandni,

00:03:29.526 --> 00:03:32.767
this you put in a Thermos,
you drink it all day.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.570
- When you open it up,

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.612
you can see the clove and the cardamom,

00:03:35.612 --> 00:03:36.685
and I think there's even a slice of ginger

00:03:36.685 --> 00:03:38.030
floating in here.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.369
I love that.

00:03:39.369 --> 00:03:40.899
- The chai, how would give it out of five?

00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:41.732
- Four.

00:03:41.732 --> 00:03:43.572
The method of cooking it different.

00:03:43.572 --> 00:03:44.951
The other maker, a stove.

00:03:44.951 --> 00:03:46.881
This one, a little bit different.

00:03:46.881 --> 00:03:47.835
- To me, it's a five, right?

00:03:47.835 --> 00:03:49.337
The chai is great,

00:03:49.337 --> 00:03:51.655
and just being in that cozy cramped space,

00:03:51.655 --> 00:03:53.958
just surrounded by smells of home,

00:03:53.958 --> 00:03:54.918
it's a five for me.

00:03:54.918 --> 00:03:56.621
- This is really, really good.

00:03:56.621 --> 00:03:58.723
I would give it maybe a 4.5.

00:03:58.723 --> 00:03:59.941
But what's amazing about it is,

00:03:59.941 --> 00:04:01.978
they're in such a small location.

00:04:01.978 --> 00:04:03.635
- But still, it's one dollar.

00:04:03.635 --> 00:04:06.193
- One dollar!
- One dollar, fresh tea.

00:04:06.193 --> 00:04:07.690
One dollar, okay.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.685
- Okay, so, because it's New York,

00:04:09.685 --> 00:04:11.071
Zainab had to leave for an appointment,

00:04:11.071 --> 00:04:13.860
so it's just me and Jamil
Uncle for the last place.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.617
You said you wanted to come in to Haandi.

00:04:15.617 --> 00:04:16.654
Why did you want to go in?

00:04:16.654 --> 00:04:18.575
- The owner and the other
guy who works over there,

00:04:18.575 --> 00:04:19.408
they know me.

00:04:19.408 --> 00:04:21.624
So I hope we're gonna meet them.

00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:22.592
Special tea for us.

00:04:22.592 --> 00:04:24.331
- (laughs) That is the key!

00:04:24.331 --> 00:04:26.826
You get better stuff. (laughs)

00:04:26.826 --> 00:04:29.883
If you know the people, or
if you're of the background.

00:04:29.883 --> 00:04:33.133
(Middle Eastern music)

00:04:39.007 --> 00:04:39.840
- [Jamil] What did you want over here?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:40.892
- Well, what kind of chai
would you drink here?

00:04:40.892 --> 00:04:42.628
- Oh, just a good chai you saw here.

00:04:42.628 --> 00:04:43.461
- Dudh patti, or...

00:04:43.461 --> 00:04:45.076
- [Jamil] Dudh patti,
let's try the dudh patti.

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:46.777
- All right, we'll get some milky...

00:04:46.777 --> 00:04:48.183
I'm gonna have him do the ordering.

00:04:48.183 --> 00:04:49.034
And speak in Urdu.

00:04:49.034 --> 00:04:50.897
My Urdu is okay, but
his is gonna be better.

00:04:50.897 --> 00:04:54.372
(speaking foreign language)

00:04:54.372 --> 00:04:56.022
- All the time, I bother him, you know.

00:04:56.022 --> 00:04:57.776
(laughing)

00:04:57.776 --> 00:04:59.451
- We've got three different
types of chai here.

00:04:59.451 --> 00:05:01.420
We got the regular tea on the left.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.476
We got the dudh patti tea in the middle.

00:05:03.476 --> 00:05:05.250
And we're gonna see the
kashmeri chai downstairs.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.766
You might not believe me,
but it's basically green tea,

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:10.921
that when you stir it for hours
and hours and hours on end,

00:05:10.921 --> 00:05:13.298
it oxidizes and becomes pink.

00:05:13.298 --> 00:05:15.364
Oh my gosh! (laughs)

00:05:15.364 --> 00:05:17.171
Oh, I got some pink on my pants.

00:05:17.171 --> 00:05:19.007
Okay, there we go.

00:05:19.007 --> 00:05:20.303
That requires some expertise.

00:05:20.303 --> 00:05:22.303
Oh my God, it's so pink!

00:05:24.435 --> 00:05:27.120
Jamil Uncle is opening
up his dudh patti chai.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.932
We got seikh kababs, chicken kababs,

00:05:29.932 --> 00:05:32.007
qormas, samosas.

00:05:32.007 --> 00:05:33.150
They just gave it to us.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.112
Because that's the way
Pakistanis do, I guess.

00:05:35.112 --> 00:05:37.123
We're gonna start with
the dudh patti chai.

00:05:37.123 --> 00:05:39.126
It's your favorite, right?
- It's my favorite.

00:05:39.126 --> 00:05:40.952
The color is really good.

00:05:40.952 --> 00:05:45.325
(speaking foreign language)

00:05:45.325 --> 00:05:46.158
- Yeah.

00:05:46.158 --> 00:05:46.991
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:46.991 --> 00:05:47.979
- This is my chai.
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:48.812
There's no spice, right?

00:05:48.812 --> 00:05:50.229
- [Jamil] No spice here, yeah.

00:05:50.229 --> 00:05:51.208
- Just good tea.

00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:52.041
- Good tea, yeah.

00:05:52.041 --> 00:05:53.034
A little extra milk, you know.

00:05:53.034 --> 00:05:53.867
- A little extra milk.

00:05:53.867 --> 00:05:54.700
- A little bit extra, you know.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.827
- The texture is amazing.

00:05:55.827 --> 00:05:57.660
The texture is definitely the best of all

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.909
of the three we've had.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:02.605
How would you rate your chai out of five?

00:06:02.605 --> 00:06:05.178
- Five.
(laughing)

00:06:05.178 --> 00:06:06.154
- I don't think about this chai,

00:06:06.154 --> 00:06:09.342
but it is really, really
reminds me of home.

00:06:09.342 --> 00:06:11.898
I want to give it 4.5, though.

00:06:11.898 --> 00:06:14.361
I don't know, it's kind
of a five, to be honest.

00:06:14.361 --> 00:06:15.574
It's a five, let's be honest.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:16.407
Very comfortable tea.

00:06:16.407 --> 00:06:19.692
I could drink it all day, honestly.

00:06:19.692 --> 00:06:21.234
So we recorded a conversation

00:06:21.234 --> 00:06:23.577
with Jamil Uncle, also, for the podcast.

00:06:23.577 --> 00:06:26.997
You can find that at
buzzfeed.com/seesomethingsaysomething.

00:06:26.997 --> 00:06:28.876
Talk about New York and
the cab driver life.

00:06:28.876 --> 00:06:30.498
Rate us on iTunes and subscribe,

00:06:30.498 --> 00:06:31.504
and we're gonna do a lot more videos

00:06:31.504 --> 00:06:32.625
like this in the future.

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:35.292
(hip hop music)

